6. Http session?
Session is stored in server. If initial interaction, server create a new session and return the sessionId into browser,
or return the existed sessionId back to browser. For all subsequent requests, browser send the sessionId back as
request header to server so server can retrieve the data for this specific user.

7. Cookie?
Cookie is stored in browser. It is created by server,It is a piece of data, containing sessionId, user preference
and everytime interaction, browser send the cookie along with requests to server.

