11. Spring security filter?
We have SecurityFilterChain to make authentication and authorization. WIth the chain, we verify the user and their
behaviors step by step to protect apps. Usually, we authenticate a user to see whether you are logged in, and from
sessionId or token to see whether you are a valid user, if you send a request, we will check whether you have the
authority to do it. Spring boot security auto config these filters for us, so I just need to add the following
methods.
Example: .formLogin(), .csrf(), .logout().

12. Bearer token and jwt?
Bearer token is a String containing user information, server parse the token to validate the user and check whether
the user is authorized to do something.
JWT is a type of bearer token. It allows user to visit various apps with single sign in. Server use the share secret
key to parse JWT to check whether jwt is not changed.

13. How to store sensitive data in database?
We don't store plain text of password in database, instead, we append a salt to the password and then hash the
code, such hashcode can't be hashed back. Salt is to make even two people have same password still get different
hashcode. When user enter password, we hash the input and compare the hashcode with what we have in database.
If match, we can validate the user.

15. Disadvantage of session?
Session is stored in the server, so I can only interact with the specific server. If in a distributed system, and
that server is out of work, I lose my state. So in modern development, token becomes very popular, such token
is stored in browser and any server that share the secret key can parse to token and than to verify the user.

